  "description": "Built around weight, developed for performance. The all-new FALCN RS 2.0 is Ridley’s latest lightweight road race platform, combining a 705 g carbon frame with refined aerodynamics and progressive race geometry. The bike was developed in close collaboration with Uno-X Mobility and tested at WorldTour level. The 12% weight reduction compared with the previous generation was achieved by revisiting the carbon lay-up, strategically redistributing material and removing unnecessary overlap. At the same time, lateral stiffness remains at the level expected from a modern aero race bike. The components were selected according to the same philosophy, including a lightweight aero seatpost and integrated Nimbus Pro cockpit. The geometry was developed based on feedback from Uno-X riders, bike fitters and thousands of kilometres of WorldTour racing. The 76° seat tube angle places the rider more centrally over the bottom bracket, while the longer reach and higher stack create a more open hip angle. The lower bottom bracket contributes to greater stability at higher speeds. The result is a modern race bike that feels light and reactive without compromising aerodynamic efficiency, stability or comfort. In its lightest configuration, the complete FALCN RS 2.0 weighs just 6.2 kg, while its Aero-to-Weight approach keeps the bike competitive on flat and rolling roads as well.",
